From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 997: an empty AP MLD Config TLV is not a teardown order

A controller with no `config mld` sections sends an AP MLD Config TLV with
num_mlds=0 on every autoconfig. The agent treats that as an instruction to
delete its own MLD configuration: it strips mld_id from every ap section in
both mapagent and wireless, then calls uci_delete_mld_config() and
clean_all_mlds(), which remove apmld0, apmld1 and stamld0.

That is fatal, and not in an obvious way. With stamld0 gone a->bstamld is
NULL, so the guard at backhaul.c:102

	if (a->bstamld && !a->cfg.physical_mld)
		return;

no longer returns early. dynbh_bsta_disable_lower_priority() then runs the
shell helper against affiliated bSTAs that no longer have a netdev, the
agent reloads its config and dies. procd restarts it, it dies again:

  procd: Instance mapagent::instance1 s in a crash loop 8 crashes, 1 seconds since last crash

Measured on hardware 2026-07-28 on a node whose MLO backhaul was healthy at
that moment -- two links, 5 GHz + 6 GHz, carrying data. The node was simply
absent from the mesh (num_nodes=2) because its agent could not stay up.
Restoring apmld0/apmld1/stamld0 by hand brought the agent back immediately
with nothing else changed.

Local MLD configuration on this platform is generated by map_genconfig and
owned by the node, not handed down by the controller. A controller that does
not know about MLD must not be able to dismantle it. Treat an empty TLV as a
no-op.

Note this is the defensive half. The controller side -- teaching it to emit
real MLD config -- is a separate change, and this patch is what makes it safe
to attempt: a controller that regresses to num_mlds=0 can no longer take the
agents down with it.

--- a/src/agent_map.c
+++ b/src/agent_map.c
@@ -2083,21 +2083,21 @@
 	offset++;
 
 	if (num_mlds == 0) {
-		list_for_each_entry(apcfg, &a->cfg.aplist, list) {
-			if (!apcfg->mld_id)
-				continue;
-			uci_set_wireless_interface_option("mapagent", "ap",
-							  "ifname", apcfg->name,
-							  "mld_id", "");
-			uci_set_wireless_interface_option("wireless",
-							  "wifi-iface",
-							  "ifname", apcfg->name,
-							  "mld", "");
-			apcfg->mld_id = 0;
-		}
-		uci_delete_mld_config(&a->cfg);
-		clean_all_mlds(&a->cfg);
-		a->cfg.num_mld = 0;
+		/* An empty AP MLD Config TLV is not an instruction to tear
+		 * down what this node configured for itself. A controller
+		 * that knows nothing about MLD sends num_mlds=0 on every
+		 * autoconfig, and the teardown below then deletes apmld*,
+		 * stamld0 and every mld_id -- after which a->bstamld is NULL,
+		 * the guard in dynbh_bsta_disable_lower_priority() no longer
+		 * returns early, and the agent dies in a crash loop. Measured
+		 * on hardware 2026-07-28: the node had a healthy two-link MLO
+		 * backhaul at the time.
+		 *
+		 * Local MLD configuration is owned by map_genconfig, not by
+		 * the controller, so an empty TLV is a no-op here.
+		 */
+		dbg("%s: empty AP MLD Config TLV -- keeping local MLD config\n",
+		    __func__);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
